 "note": "the impulse response buffer is compared with X_ITE 16.6.0 (channels, length = samples / channels, a sample value), then normalize, the input stage and the clock. Web Audio takes 1, 2 or 4 channels only (3 is not tested: X_ITE throws on it). Runs on the real clock for start and stop.",
 "gaps": [
  "three channels, or more than four, are refused by Web Audio; the bridge keeps the previous response (X_ITE throws)",
  "the response is built at the audio context's own sample rate, as in X_ITE; the processed sound is not compared",
  "numberOfChannels is a Convolver field in X_ITE 16.6.0 but is not in the X3D 4.0 UOM or XSD; the bridge has it as in X_ITE (set at run time only, since the XSD cannot write it)"
